d.add_heading('Matched validation ranking',1);table(d,['Model','RMSE mean ± SD','MAE','R squared','Direction','Gain vs E0'],[[n,f'{r.rmse_mean:.6f} ± {r.rmse_std:.6f}',f'{r.mae_mean:.6f}',f'{r.r2_mean:.6f}',f'{100*r.directional_accuracy_mean:.2f}%',f'{r.rmse_improvement_vs_E0_percent:+.3f}%'] for n,r in rank.iterrows()]+[['Persistence',f'{pers["rmse"]:.6f}',f'{pers["mae"]:.6f}',f'{pers["r2"]:.6f}','No change','—']]);d.add_paragraph('All models use the same 2,136 validation origins. E0 is technical only; E1 archived direct news; E1B compact direct news; E2_h6 the six-hour equation; E3 combined direct and equation inputs. E4 freezes E0 and learns a small news correction. Mean and sample SD describe five seeds, not independent markets. Smaller RMSE/MAE is better; positive gain means lower RMSE than E0.');pic(d,R/'RANKING.png','Error bars are seed SD, not confidence intervals. The vertical axis is truncated to show small differences.');d.add_paragraph(f'The ungated correction has {100*(rank.loc["E4_ungated","rmse_mean"]/rank.loc["E1B","rmse_mean"]-1):.3f}% higher RMSE than E1B; gated has {100*(rank.loc["E4_gated","rmse_mean"]/rank.loc["E1B","rmse_mean"]-1):.3f}% higher RMSE. E1B remains the validation-selected configuration.')
pageheading(d,'Uncertainty and stability');d.add_paragraph(stat_e4);table(d,['Contrast','Risk difference','Adjusted interval'],[[r.candidate.replace('E4_','')+' vs '+r.reference.replace('E4_',''),f'{r.rmse_risk_difference:+.6f}',f'[{r.ci_adjusted_low:+.6f}, {r.ci_adjusted_high:+.6f}]'] for _,r in ci[ci.block_hours.eq(72)].iterrows()]);d.add_paragraph('All seven primary adjusted intervals include zero. The gated-minus-ungated estimate is positive, favouring ungated numerically, but its interval also includes zero. The full 95% intervals and 24/168-hour sensitivities are saved in the analysis folder. Numerical gains do not establish a robust forecasting benefit.');pic(d,R/'MONTHLY.png','Calendar-month comparisons are descriptive; December 2025 and March 2026 are partial segments.');d.add_paragraph('Temporal overlap and shared market conditions mean these month segments are not independent experiments. The repeated use of validation to select configurations and epochs must be acknowledged before any generalisation claim.')
pageheading(d,'Design safeguards and interpretation');d.add_paragraph(protocol);d.add_paragraph(training_e4);d.add_paragraph('Both E4 variants reuse eight E3 news inputs with the six-hour equation; there is no new scoring, timestamp shift or additional sentiment feature. The correction starts at zero. The gated model has 1,282 trainable parameters and the ungated model 1,265, each in addition to 564,353 frozen parameters. The ungated ablation retains the correction encoder and fixes the gate to one. Gate-disabled predictions reuse E0 and require no training.')
d.add_heading('What the gate analysis can establish',1);d.add_paragraph('Every validation origin has eligible trailing-48-hour news. No natural mask-off group exists, so this period cannot establish whether the learned gate prevents unnecessary corrections during genuinely news-inactive periods. Forced-mask tests confirm the software safeguard, not predictive effectiveness in missing market regimes. Current-hour news and no-new-article subgroups are reported separately in each model report. Gate values and correction magnitudes describe model behaviour, not causal effects.')
d.add_heading('Limitations and decision',1);d.add_paragraph(limits_e4);d.add_paragraph('Retain E1B as the current validation winner. Neither adding the equation directly nor using a gated residual correction has demonstrated improvement over it. Preserve all negative and positive results. A genuinely separate chronological replication or reserved evaluation is needed before claiming that any configuration generalises. No new HBAR, rolling, timing, fine-tuning or evaluation runs were started.')
